 @iamawatcher9201  I have seen a lot of people making the difference between apology and being sorry, I want to say something, (not to defend Will, I think is pretty clear this is some damage control and Im not into his head to know if he has really thought about what he did).
This is my point, I dont think being sorry is a "better" way to mend things you have done bad, I do think its more genuine and can help you to take the necessary steps to make things right. But i also think that someone that does look back and sees what he did was wrong and takes the time to say damn , that thing i did was a mistake , even if they are not sorry, the fact that they look back and try to do what they think is right its also good for me. Because in the end being sorry is a feeling and people feel differently, some people think some tears are enough, others think you should whip yourself. So thats why I think , if u realise that what you did was wrong even if It doesnt mess up your sleep, to me its valid. 
Also forgive my english, Im spanish so its not my first language. Let me now what you think <3

